      "content": "1.1 Overview"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Odisha (formerly Orissa) is a state on the eastern coast of India. It is bordered by the Bay of Bengal to the east, making it a maritime state with a long coastline. It was carved as a separate province on 1 April 1936, making it the first state in India to be formed on a linguistic basis. That date is celebrated as Utkal Dibasa (Odisha Day / Odisha Foundation Day).",
      "id": "jgtue8j"
    },
